  "2026-10-23T23:21:44.507Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-10-24: canonical orientation, request-specific SDK/rollback search, fresh open and in_progress lists, and complete strict all-status read of 3083 items including 2799 closed and 14 canceled; no omissions or unreadable files. Exact GitHub issue and title checks found no existing owner for this delta. Closed SDK/bulk foundations were read live and remain completed. Source report retained in full; intake is not reproduction proof."
  "2026-10-24T09:41:59.524Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: remove schema materialization from shared settings reads while retaining explicit init scaffolding. Prove absence and byte preservation across SDK and CLI reads, including refused reads, and preserve custom workflow loading. Related completed read-only fixes remain terminal; this is the independently reported missing-file delta."
  "2026-10-24T09:48:23.845Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: the same isolated fixture failed before the fix because the first SDK get recreated workflows.json. Removing read-time scaffold from settings hydration preserves absence for get/list/context/search and refused get in SDK and CLI, plus existing schema bytes. Explicit init repairs missing workflow seeds, and reads tolerate a wholly absent optional schema directory. Cache, hook and malformed-schema tests are updated to assert pure reads and explicit owned fixture setup."
  "2026-10-24T10:08:10.993Z","harness:codex","Full-suite boundary audit found read-bootstrap assumptions in config, telemetry identity and transaction-preview tests. Updated them to retain their identity/history/consent/migration assertions while requiring unrelated missing schema files to remain absent. A genuine migration regression was also caught: reading a missing optional type file before validation leaked ENOENT. Migration now reads the optional snapshot in memory and preserves the existing typed missing-custom-definition refusal without recreating the file. The regression asserts both refusal and absence. New read-context tests moved into the existing read-output area to preserve the120-file directory cap; public extension guidance stays within its450-line budget."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T10:49:09.540Z","harness:codex","Optional schema hydration is a read boundary. Keep defaults in memory, retain missing-file signatures in cache invalidation, and test dependent mutation preflight so removing hidden bootstrap writes cannot leak raw filesystem errors."
